Commutators with diag(2,4) generate SL2(F7); hence its derived group is the whole group.
Normal closure of diag(2,4), order3, is SL2(F7); every prime-to3 quotient is trivial.
Wild matrix diag(2,4) has order3; Frobenius diag(3,1) has determinant3 and commutes with it.
Neither quadratic scalar removes the nontrivial order3 inertia.
